Description:

iTIP scheduling messages are delivered after the request which caused them has
finished with the organizer's calendar, so an organizer and a local attendee
acting on each other's calendars at once no longer deadlock.  For CalDAV, each
attendee's SCHEDULE-STATUS is written to the stored resource in a second store
afterwards, so a scheduling PUT no longer returns an ETag - clients must re-read
the resource, as they already must when default alarms rewrite it.


